Subject: armGBA: a reclaim's unlinked jumps reach the instruction cache in one
 kernel call on the 3DS (jitHostFlushBatch), and the list of cartridge blocks
 and the other slots' lists are passed over with a filter of the blocks going
 away, so a block that isn't one isn't read (a cache miss each; with a kernel
 call a jump, these were most of a 13-25 ms reclaim in Final Fantasy VI on a
 New 2DS XL)


